{
 "voiceover": "[excited, conversational] Wait — Apple spent years dismissing touchscreen Macs, and it just launched one. [curious] It's the MacBook Pro with PROLED XDR Display, Apple's first laptop with a touch screen. Apple says the touch sensor is built into the display itself, which should cut lag.\n\n[intrigued, building energy] It comes in 14-inch and 16-inch versions, starting at $2,899 and $3,399. It runs on an M5 Pro or M5 Max chip, ships November 6, and pre-orders are open.\n\n[amused] Back in 2016, Apple's Phil Schiller told WIRED you \"can't optimize for both\" touch and a trackpad. [serious] Now Apple says many existing apps work right away, because touches register as clicks. And it says it's \"only getting started\" on macOS touch.\n\n[confident] If you're a designer, musician or developer, this one's aimed at you.\n\n[playful, warm] Send this to the friend who swore Macs would never get touch.",
